Supporting materials for the ACL2 Workshop 2026 paper

  Pablo Oscar Cayuela
  Mechanized Formal Verification of q-Pulse Rectifier Voltage Equations
  Using ACL2

Mechanical verification, in ACL2(r), of exact values and cross-checks of
the closed-form average and RMS output voltage equations of q-pulse
rectifiers (uncontrolled, fully controlled and semi-controlled), based on
the sampling function Sa(x) = sin(x)/x. Thirteen theorems in three books.
The development version is at
https://github.com/pcayuela/ACL2-rectifiers-check

Books:

  00-sampling-function.lisp          Sa and its exact values
  01-topology-instantiation.lisp     instantiation of the master equations
                                     per topology; the two findings
  02-semiconverter-cross-checks.lisp the three semi-converter cross-checks
  top.lisp                           includes the three books

All books require the ACL2(r) executable and are marked
"cert_param: (uses-acl2r)".
